| `RETRACTED` | — | *(none — absorbing)* |

### 4.3 Three properties the topology is built to guarantee

**P1 — No node ever leaves the graph.** There is no `DELETED` status and no edge out of
`RETRACTED`. Deletion is expressible only as a transition *into* `RETRACTED`, which requires a
`retraction` block naming who retracted it, when, why, and on what evidence. This is the structural
form of the goal's "deleted node" invariant; `I08`, `I09`, `I10`, and `I11` attack it from four
directions (`fixture-corpus.md` §3).

**P2 — Promotion is never free.** Every edge requires a `basis` from a closed epistemic enum and
≥1 `evidence_refs` entry. There is no edge whose basis may be a count. (§5.3.)

**P3 — Quarantine is reversible, retraction is not.** `QUARANTINED` exists so that discovering bad
*evidence* (the `CANARY-0001`/`CANARY-0002` situation) does not force a verdict on the *claim*.
`adversary_cleared` returns the node to `ACTIVE` or `CANDIDATE`; `falsification` moves it to the
tombstone. Collapsing these would mean every forged-evidence catch permanently destroys a possibly-
true claim.

### 4.4 How the machine is encoded in L1

```jsonc
"$defs": {
  "legal_transition": {
    "$comment": "INV-FSM-1: (from,to) must be a legal edge; RETRACTED is absorbing",
    "anyOf": [
      { "properties": { "from": {"const":"PROPOSED"},  "to": {"const":"CANDIDATE"} } },
      { "properties": { "from": {"const":"PROPOSED"},  "to": {"const":"QUARANTINED"} } },
      // ... 17 more, one per row of §4.2 ...
      { "properties": { "from": {"const":"SUPERSEDED"},"to": {"const":"RETRACTED"} } }
    ]
  }
}
```

`RETRACTED` needs no explicit rule: it appears in no `from` position, so any promotion out of it
fails `anyOf`. The basis↔transition binding of §4.2's third column is a parallel `allOf` of
`if (from,to) then basis ∈ {...}` clauses, carrying `$comment: "INV-FSM-2: ..."`.

> **Implementation note.** `anyOf` produces a poor error message (it reports the whole branch set).
> The `Violation` mapper should special-case `anyOf` failures whose `schema_pointer` starts with
> `/$defs/legal_transition` and emit pointer `/promotion` with keyword `anyOf` — the manifest
> expectations for `I11`/`I17` are written against that normalised form.

